+# NINE65 innovation inventory and return paths
+
+Source snapshot: `88a7bdadbf0e1f8fbfdb2b37e9843101b8db3484`; inspected 2026-11-12. This is a source-based research inventory, not a new whole-workspace execution certificate. The linked Codex task could not be read because this session exposes no `read_thread` tool; its title supplies no evidence for this inventory.
+
+The strongest organizing opportunity is a **query-aware exact-computation layer**: a consumer specifies what it needs to know, a producer supplies authentic observations sufficient for that query, and the implementation transports the query without first materializing every underlying coordinate. This applies to arithmetic, trajectories, clocks, invariants and application aggregates. K-Elimination is a particularly cheap constructor in that larger layer. The constructions below identify concrete opportunities to connect existing work, including connections that feed back into CRAM itself.
+
+## Scope and evidence method
+
+I enumerated `crates/`, `docs/`, `research/` and `verified-innovations/`, read the current architecture/status/claim guidance, and inspected source definitions and representative implementations in the arithmetic, exact-transcendental, MANA/UNHAL, Clockwork, QMNF, application and lifecycle families. This is a family-level inventory with selected call-chain inspection, not a claim that every repository line or every archived experiment was audited. Code and current scope notes take precedence over old module banners. No new Rust tests or Lean proofs were run for this document.
+
+The historical [14-innovation validation summary](../../verified-innovations/docs/VALIDATION_SUMMARY.md) is useful as a discovery index, but it explicitly includes admitted Coq proofs and broad performance claims. The maintained proof system is Lean. A file's presence under `verified-innovations` does not by itself establish its theorem assumptions, current implementation refinement, speedup or cryptographic security. The current [claim ledger](../../docs/CLAIM_EVIDENCE_LEDGER.md), [public-refresh status](../../docs/PUBLIC_REFRESH_STATUS.md), and [CRAM repair record](../../docs/execution/2026-11-12/CRAM_PATH_REPAIR.md) provide finer evidence scopes.
+
+The user's current architectural instruction is retained: derive K on demand from authentic state; do not turn the intended substrate into a persistent scalar-winding ledger. Existing adapters that store winding remain useful reference implementations, but are not the intended on-demand execution path.
+
+## Inventory
+
+| Contribution family | Mathematical primitive and current source | What it enables; what comes back into CRAM |
+|---|---|---|
